    "result_text": "All references are consistent. The change is complete and the full test suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI made `householdId` deterministic and reworked household duplicate handling across the `POST /api/owners` pipeline:\n\n**`OwnerIdentity.householdId`** \u2014 changed signature from `(lastName, address)` to `(lastName, postcode)`. It now computes the **first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode`**, and returns `null` when no postcode is given (no household can form). Owners with the same last name + postcode therefore resolve to the same value automatically.\n\n**`AssignHouseholdId`** \u2014 now unconditionally stamps the deterministic id from the built owner's last name + postcode. Removed the old behaviour where it only ran on `sharesHousehold` and mutated existing housemates to \"link\" them \u2014 there is nothing to link anymore.\n\n**`RequireUniqueIdentity`** (the duplicate block) \u2014 computes the would-be `householdId` the same way (always, not gated on the flag) and rejects **409** on either an exact `identityKey` match *or* a **household duplicate** (an existing owner with the same computed `householdId`). The household rejection is bypassed only when `sharesHousehold: true`, admitting the owner as a declared household member.\n\n**`FlagPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 a declared household member (`sharesHousehold: true`) is now left unflagged: it sets `possibleDuplicate = false` and returns early, since its shared last name/postcode is exactly what it declared.\n\n**`CountHouseholdMembers`** \u2014 unchanged logic (still keys off the now-deterministic `householdId`); doc updated to reflect that housemates already share the id rather than being linked.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `householdId` and `sharesHousehold` field descriptions to match the new semantics.\n\nBehaviour now matches the spec: same last name + postcode \u2192 same `householdId`; a second such owner is a 409 household duplicate unless it sets `sharesHousehold`, in which case it's created as a declared member and not flagged as a possible duplicate. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
